#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region

#% text
# `region(r)` marks the region `r` as a region; it stays as it is, and every region function reads through it.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The regions are the primitives `point`, `line`, `polygon`, `triangle`, `tetrahedron`, `simplex`, `disk`, `circle`, `ball`, `sphere`, `ellipsoid`, `rectangle`, `cuboid`, and `interval`, `implicit_region` and `parametric_region`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A disk as a region:

#% cell
region(disk([0, 0], 2))
#% output
#= region(disk([0, 0], 2))

#% text
# Region functions read through it:

#% cell
region_measure(region(disk([0, 0], 2)))
#% output
#= 4*pi

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `implicit_region`, `region_measure`, `region_plot`
